<title>BELGIUM: CITY HOTELS CLOSES BOND, WARRANT ISSUE.</title>
<headline>CITY HOTELS CLOSES BOND, WARRANT ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian hotels-to-airlines group City Hotels SA said in a statement on Tuesday its one billion Belgian franc issue of bonds with warrants attached had been oversubscribed and was being closed a day ahead of schedule.</p>
<p>&quot;The way (the issue) will be shared out (among applicants) will be communicated by February 22 at the latest,&quot; City Hotels said.</p>
<p>The funding raised from the issue, which was launched on February 13 and was due to run until Wednesday, has been earmarked to expand the group's U.S. hotels business.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
